  "applies_to": "Unipi Extension xS51 RS-485 module per the Unipi Extension xS51 Modbus map v2.0.",
  "summary": "The Unipi Extension xS51 is an RS-485 Modbus RTU extension module with 4 digital inputs, 5 relay outputs, 4 analog outputs (0-10 V) and 4 configurable analog inputs (voltage, current or resistance). The map covers I/O states, analog values, counters, the master watchdog and configuration.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 15,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The map lists each register in decimal and hex starting at 0; the number is the wire address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Extension xS51 Modbus map",
    "doc_number": "v2.0",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://kb.unipi.technology/_media/files:products:extensions:unipi-extension-xs51-modbus-map-v2.0.pdf",
    "pages": "holding registers, coils and description sheets"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the description sheet states 16-bit values are big endian (AB) and 32-bit values are mid-little endian (CDAB, low word first).",
    "Registers marked Reserved - Do Not Use are left out.",
    "Baud codes for the RS-485 configuration register: 11 = 2400, 12 = 4800, 13 = 9600, 14 = 19200, 15 = 38400, 4097 = 57600, 4098 = 115200 bps."
  ],
